WEBVTT

00:00:05.459 --> 00:00:08.960
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the 23rd. Have we got everybody on?</v>

00:00:10.689 --> 00:00:16.640
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, morning. The heating in the portakabin has apparently decided it's spring already. Absolutely Baltic in here.</v>

00:00:17.829 --> 00:00:22.030
<v Jamie Brennan>That's why you've got the coat zipped up to your eyebrows, then.</v>

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.699
<v Callum Reid>Exactly. Just having a moan, before anyone puts it on a list.</v>

00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:36.009
<v Priya Raman>Morning. Am I coming through all right? Teams has picked a different microphone again.</v>

00:00:37.689 --> 00:00:38.890
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, you're clear.</v>

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.939
<v Marcus Hale>Louder than the rest of us, if anything.</v>

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:50.149
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, let's get into it. A few things to agree this morning.</v>

00:00:50.659 --> 00:00:55.560
<v Callum Reid>Just before that, already swapped the filter on the Stretch Wrapper yesterday. That's done.</v>

00:00:57.039 --> 00:01:00.539
<v Hannah Price>Ah, lovely. I wasn't sure whether that had actually happened.</v>

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:05.180
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, all sorted yesterday. Nothing needed on that today.</v>

00:01:07.019 --> 00:01:13.670
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers. Whitty, can you send the shift handover report round by the 28th? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.959
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, so, the report itself? We're not talking about a new format as well?</v>

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:25.939
<v Sarah Okafor>No, just send the shift handover report round. No redesign.</v>

00:01:28.159 --> 00:01:32.709
<v David Whitfield>Fine, I'll send it round by the 28th. Understood, important rather than urgent.</v>

00:01:34.109 --> 00:01:37.609
<v Jamie Brennan>You looked worried there. Nearly had to choose a font.</v>

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.829
<v David Whitfield>That's how it starts, mate. Then suddenly you've got twelve tabs.</v>

00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:49.450
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you sort the training records for the new starters today? Low priority.</v>

00:01:50.969 --> 00:01:54.120
<v Jamie Brennan>Today, yeah? Just checking because you said low priority.</v>

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:01.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, still today. Low priority within today, not one to push everything else out for.</v>

00:02:01.629 --> 00:02:05.829
<v Jamie Brennan>Got you. I'll sort the training records for the new starters today.</v>

00:02:06.709 --> 00:02:10.909
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, the records side can look tiny until you actually open it.</v>

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:16.009
<v Jamie Brennan>Don't say that. I'm choosing to remain optimistic.</v>

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:24.080
<v Sarah Okafor>Tommo, can you run the monthly fire alarm test by Wednesday? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:02:25.349 --> 00:02:28.849
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, I'll run the monthly fire alarm test by Wednesday.</v>

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.699
<v Marcus Hale>Monthly already? Feels like February's only just started.</v>

00:02:35.789 --> 00:02:41.039
<v Sarah Okafor>I know. But Wednesday's the limit on that one, even though it's not an emergency.</v>

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.759
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. It won't get lost at the bottom.</v>

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:50.389
<v Priya Raman>February cheats. Same amount of stuff, fewer days.</v>

00:02:52.439 --> 00:02:54.889
<v Tomasz Nowak>Doesn't seem to mean fewer meetings, though.</v>

00:02:56.039 --> 00:03:03.039
<v Tomasz Nowak>While I've got the mic, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the Atlas tomorrow. Normal priority for that.</v>

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.590
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Tommo. Tomorrow, normal priority, agreed.</v>

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:16.240
<v Hannah Price>Mm, the wording on those matters. Everyone thinks they mean the same thing until they're stood in front of it.</v>

00:03:17.539 --> 00:03:24.889
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, exactly. Needs to make sense to the person doing the work, not just the person reading it at a desk.</v>

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:31.590
<v David Whitfield>Especially when it's a wall of text. You lose the actual risk in all the words.</v>

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:36.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. There's one more, and this is the one that comes first.</v>

00:03:37.379 --> 00:03:43.330
<v Sarah Okafor>Tom, can you replace the seals on the GT2 inlet valve today at 2pm? Top priority please.</v>

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:48.379
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, you broke up just on the time. Today at two?</v>

00:03:48.819 --> 00:03:54.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Today at 2pm, yes. Replace the seals on the GT2 inlet valve. Top priority please.</v>

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:58.430
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, that one's the main concern from the plant side.</v>

00:03:59.039 --> 00:04:06.389
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, I've got you now. I'll replace the seals on the GT2 inlet valve today at 2pm. That's my top priority.</v>

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:10.750
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, makes sense to put that ahead of the paperwork.</v>

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:17.149
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. The other dates we've agreed still stand, but that gets first call.</v>

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:22.959
<v Jamie Brennan>Definitely not going to argue that training records outrank that.</v>

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.589
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good, because I've only got the one pair of hands, despite popular belief.</v>

00:04:29.939 --> 00:04:35.540
<v Priya Raman>You were clear that time, by the way. Think it was just a little Teams wobble.</v>

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:40.680
<v Hannah Price>Same here. Lost half a second, then it came back.</v>

00:04:41.889 --> 00:04:44.339
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Anything unclear about what we've agreed?</v>

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:48.310
<v Hannah Price>No, all clear from me.</v>

00:04:49.439 --> 00:04:51.889
<v Callum Reid>Same. Nothing else from production this morning.</v>

00:04:52.189 --> 00:04:55.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Thanks, everyone. I'll let you get back to it.</v>

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.240
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers, all.</v>
